1
00:01:38,190 --> 00:01:44,030
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:46,880
[Episode 19]

3
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:49,360
[Starry Night] [Prosperous Dynasty]

4
00:01:49,430 --> 00:01:55,259
[Kindly close the door behind you]

5
00:01:55,289 --> 00:01:58,229
[Medical Staff Only]

6
00:01:58,350 --> 00:02:06,550
[Quiet]

7
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:00,870
Hello.

8
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,840
I'm Wang Chao, deputy chief

9
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,480
of the
Municipal Criminal Investigation Division.

10
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,200
Doctor,

11
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,070
how's Du Fang doing?

12
00:02:07,590 --> 00:02:09,250
He's out of immediate danger,

13
00:02:09,310 --> 00:02:10,080
but it's too early

14
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,470
to tell how well

15
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,680
he'll recover.

16
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:15,280
Now that he's alive,

17
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,590
it changes

18
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:17,800
the nature of things.

19
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:19,840
Anyway, thank you.

20
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:21,140
It's all right.

21
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:23,400
There's something
I need to ask you, though.

22
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:25,030
Before he was shot,

23
00:02:25,150 --> 00:02:27,190
the patient kept insisting
he was innocent.

24
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:28,280
That's impossible.

25
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,590
He assaulted his supervisor at work.

26
00:02:29,590 --> 00:02:31,240
Plenty of people saw it.

27
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,150
I'm not questioning your investigation.

28
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:35,190
It's just that

29
00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:36,630
during surgery,

30
00:02:36,710 --> 00:02:37,870
we discovered

31
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:39,079
a tumor

32
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,480
in the temporal lobe.

33
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,280
Damage to the temporal lobe

34
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,840
can cause personality changes,

35
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:43,840
erratic behavior,

36
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,870
and even psychiatric symptoms.

37
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,520
What does that mean?

38
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,840
That there's something wrong

39
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,030
with his brain?

40
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:52,430
That he

41
00:02:52,590 --> 00:02:54,250
didn't know what he was doing?

42
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,540
That's a possibility.

43
00:02:55,910 --> 00:02:57,400
So I'd recommend

44
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,060
having him undergo another evaluation.

45
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:09,280
[Bicycle Parking]

46
00:03:09,390 --> 00:03:10,240
[Operating Department]

47
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,240
This is Dr. Liu Zhengliang,

48
00:03:14,130 --> 00:03:23,380
[Accessible Route—Please Keep Clear]

49
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:15,840
the doctor who chose to operate

50
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,120
on a patient even

51
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,960
while being held hostage by criminals.

52
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:21,120
These two are reporters
from the provincial newspaper.

53
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,430
They'd like to do

54
00:03:22,430 --> 00:03:23,870
a feature interview with you.

55
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:24,280
Hello.

56
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,000
Hello.

57
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,430
Hi, hi.

58
00:03:28,030 --> 00:03:29,360
I've barely been back a day,

59
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,910
and I've already got so much
to deal with.

60
00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:32,520
I still have to go over everything
with Chief Physician Tong.

61
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:34,430
Can you give me a minute
to catch my breath?

62
00:03:34,430 --> 00:03:35,960
This is the Zhang family's
thank-you banner.

63
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,360
It got a little blood on it,

64
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,760
and I had them clean it up.

65
00:03:38,910 --> 00:03:41,040
Take it back and hang it in your office.

66
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:52,360
See?

67
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:56,570
This is a rare opportunity
for some good publicity.

68
00:03:59,630 --> 00:04:00,960
You know perfectly well

69
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:03,760
how much this hospital is struggling.

70
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:06,240
Guess I came back
at the worst possible time.

71
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,800
Quite the opposite.

72
00:04:08,110 --> 00:04:10,370
Didn't you save another life just today?

73
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,560
All right.

74
00:04:18,750 --> 00:04:20,149
Where do you want to talk?

75
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:22,600
How about the conference room?

76
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,330
Let's use the conference room.

77
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:25,630
Let's go.

78
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,780
Let's go. Let's go.

79
00:04:28,630 --> 00:04:29,430
Dr. Liu,

80
00:04:29,510 --> 00:04:30,310
you said earlier

81
00:04:29,670 --> 00:04:33,170
[Healing pain with compassion,
lighting up hope with dedication]

82
00:04:30,310 --> 00:04:31,950
that the fugitive's criminal behavior

83
00:04:31,950 --> 00:04:35,190
might have been caused by some kind
of physiological abnormality.

84
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:35,990
That's right.

85
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,000
Of course, it's only

86
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,040
a possibility I've raised.

87
00:04:39,159 --> 00:04:40,810
We'll need to investigate
further to verify it.

88
00:04:40,810 --> 00:04:46,940
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

89
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:43,000
If your theory turns out to be correct,

90
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,720
you'll have saved

91
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:46,240
more than one life.

92
00:04:49,830 --> 00:04:50,630
Well,

93
00:04:51,159 --> 00:04:52,159
honestly,

94
00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:54,430
I didn't think that far ahead
at the time.

95
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:55,560
You're very modest.

96
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:56,560
So, what made you

97
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:59,020
decide to become a doctor
in the first place?

98
00:05:08,070 --> 00:05:09,530
When my uncle passed away,

99
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:11,720
I realized

100
00:05:12,950 --> 00:05:14,600
how much I hated feeling helpless

101
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,920
in the face of death.

102
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:32,400
[Memorial Hall]

103
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:36,560
Well,

104
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:41,120
my college entrance exam score was
high enough to get me into medical school.

105
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:41,870
I didn't give it much thought

106
00:05:41,870 --> 00:05:43,730
when I filled out my application.

107
00:05:45,490 --> 00:05:51,310
[Medical Staff Only]

108
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,870
What are you waiting for?

109
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:57,680
For you.

110
00:05:58,070 --> 00:05:59,610
Let's grab something to eat

111
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:00,950
and celebrate.

112
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:02,750
Celebrate what?

113
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:06,310
Come on, it's a once-in-a-lifetime thing!

114
00:06:06,390 --> 00:06:07,390
Maybe the only time

115
00:06:07,390 --> 00:06:09,000
in your life

116
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,510
you'll ever operate on a patient

117
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:11,240
who's been shot in the head.

118
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:13,640
Don't you think that's worth celebrating?

119
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,360
Sure.

120
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,210
Let's invite Zhengliang, too.

121
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:19,950
The president dragged him off.

122
00:06:26,190 --> 00:06:27,520
So... just the two of us?

123
00:06:28,950 --> 00:06:29,750
Just us two.

124
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:38,040
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

125
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:36,920
I, uh... I need

126
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:38,950
to go home
and make dinner for my dad.

127
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,280
Then I'll treat you to pizza.

128
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,580
Bring your dad along, too.

129
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:56,920
[Accessible Route—Please Keep Clear]

130
00:06:56,940 --> 00:07:01,000
[To the Surgical Ward]

131
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,330
Uncle Che, you're holding it upside down.

132
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:13,750
You think I'm blind?

133
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:16,130
It's the right way up on this side.

134
00:07:17,950 --> 00:07:19,080
Go on, keep looking.

135
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:25,600
This is your second time
coming to our place,

136
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,040
but you've brought exactly

137
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,570
the same things both times.

138
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:30,430
Come clean.

139
00:07:30,630 --> 00:07:31,630
Who sent you?

140
00:07:38,070 --> 00:07:39,870
Comrade Xiaobo sent me.

141
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,720
Got it. Got it.

142
00:07:42,310 --> 00:07:43,040
Eat up.

143
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:44,800
Wait a minute.

144
00:07:47,159 --> 00:07:49,070
It's not safe to talk here anymore.

145
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:50,070
Let's step aside.

146
00:07:53,270 --> 00:07:53,870
Where are you going?

147
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:54,630
Don't ask.

148
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,830
Wait, wait.

149
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:59,040
Walls have ears.

150
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:06,640
According to the principles of cosmology,

151
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,530
the universe is nearly uniform

152
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,510
on sufficiently large scales.

153
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:12,120
The differences in matter density

154
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,050
between regions

155
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:15,090
are relatively small.

156
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,190
Matter and energy

157
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:18,870
are likely to be distributed homogeneously

158
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:21,720
and isotropically.

159
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,510
This is top secret.

160
00:08:40,669 --> 00:08:41,960
Top secret.

161
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:43,630
It's a secret between you and me.

162
00:08:43,630 --> 00:08:44,670
All right, Uncle Che.

163
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:45,910
No, call me Comrade.

164
00:08:48,150 --> 00:08:49,280
All right, Comrade.

165
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:51,670
Mingming,

166
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:55,000
I like this comrade.

167
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:00,960
Comrade.

168
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:04,670
Comrade.

169
00:09:09,390 --> 00:09:10,200
Mingming.

170
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,270
Mingming.

171
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,200
Well,

172
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,510
turn right up ahead,
and it'll be easier to get a cab there.

173
00:09:14,510 --> 00:09:15,370
I'll get going.

174
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,910
You've treated me.

175
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,320
Let me

176
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:22,080
return the favor.

177
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:25,440
Pick a time.

178
00:09:30,910 --> 00:09:32,510
Are you into me or something?

179
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:36,480
What do you mean?

180
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:38,390
We're both adults.

181
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,120
Come on, don't play dumb.

182
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:44,440
Yes.

183
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,440
I only got divorced a few months ago.

184
00:09:54,270 --> 00:09:56,470
And work's been
keeping me really busy.

185
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:58,630
I-I also have to apply for a PhD program

186
00:09:58,630 --> 00:09:59,890
and take care of my dad.

187
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:03,130
I don't want to get
into a new relationship right now.

188
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,630
You think I'm not good enough at my job?

189
00:10:07,630 --> 00:10:09,430
That I'm not impressive enough?

190
00:10:13,870 --> 00:10:15,730
A little, yeah. That's part of it.

191
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:18,630
Right.

192
00:10:20,910 --> 00:10:22,120
You're so talented,

193
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:23,960
so hardworking.

194
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,360
In your eyes,

195
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:30,000
I must be lazy,

196
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,600
just coasting through life,

197
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:33,560
with absolutely no appeal.

198
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:39,000
Got it.

199
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,390
Got what?

200
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,130
You're so used to

201
00:10:45,630 --> 00:10:46,870
being lazy,

202
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,670
but deep down,

203
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:50,600
you still want to better yourself.

204
00:10:50,670 --> 00:10:52,670
Seeing me rushing around,
working hard all day,

205
00:10:52,670 --> 00:10:53,720
fills a void

206
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:54,910
in you.

207
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:56,790
Man,

208
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:58,360
take it from me.

209
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,510
That's not love.

210
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:04,280
At best, you're looking for
what you lack in someone else.

211
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:05,750
What you need to do now

212
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,120
is work on yourself.

213
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,390
Never pin your hopes

214
00:11:08,390 --> 00:11:09,790
on someone else.

215
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,750
Got it?

216
00:11:13,790 --> 00:11:14,600
Yeah,

217
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,480
that makes sense.

218
00:11:20,670 --> 00:11:21,730
Thanks for dinner.

219
00:11:22,510 --> 00:11:23,510
See you at work.

220
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,940
Maybe I am looking for
what I lack,

221
00:11:27,870 --> 00:11:29,910
but my feelings for you are genuine.

222
00:11:30,510 --> 00:11:32,240
Just wait. I'll work on myself,

223
00:11:32,670 --> 00:11:34,910
become a better doctor,

224
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,130
and then I'll come after you again.

225
00:12:08,510 --> 00:12:09,320
I'm off.

226
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:16,050
Why are you still here?

227
00:12:17,190 --> 00:12:18,440
I'm gonna play some games.

228
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,790
I'll head out after a bit.

229
00:12:19,790 --> 00:12:22,440
Done playing?

230
00:12:22,870 --> 00:12:23,600
If you're done,

231
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:24,860
walk me home, will you?

232
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:26,790
I'm done.

233
00:12:27,150 --> 00:12:27,960
All done.

234
00:12:28,310 --> 00:12:32,800
[Traditional Massage
by Blind Practitioners]

235
00:12:28,390 --> 00:12:29,240
Let's go.

236
00:12:29,510 --> 00:12:30,840
Have you changed?

237
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:31,960
I can wait for you.

238
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:32,750
I'm ready.

239
00:12:33,390 --> 00:12:34,630
All right, let's go.

240
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:43,200
The tactile paving ends here.

241
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:44,080
Let me help you.

242
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:45,390
No need.

243
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:47,510
I know this stretch
like the back of my hand.

244
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:48,670
If I needed help with every little thing,

245
00:12:48,670 --> 00:12:50,470
I wouldn't have made it this far.

246
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,390
What's wrong with the tactile paving?

247
00:12:52,390 --> 00:12:53,790
They did such a shoddy job.

248
00:12:53,790 --> 00:12:55,600
How did the city sign off
on this construction?

249
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,150
It looks good,
but it's useless in practice.

250
00:12:57,150 --> 00:12:58,790
Well, roads are built

251
00:12:58,790 --> 00:13:00,390
to serve the majority, right?

252
00:13:00,390 --> 00:13:01,510
We're a minority,

253
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,030
so it's only natural
that we're overlooked.

254
00:13:03,030 --> 00:13:04,390
Before you met me,

255
00:13:04,390 --> 00:13:05,390
you probably never even noticed

256
00:13:05,390 --> 00:13:05,840
whether there were

257
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:08,640
blind people walking
around the streets, did you?

258
00:13:13,670 --> 00:13:14,480
I, uh...

259
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:17,580
T-There's something I'd like to ask you,

260
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:19,200
if you don't mind.

261
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:23,550
You want to know why I'm blind,

262
00:13:23,550 --> 00:13:24,240
right?

263
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,240
Yeah.

264
00:13:28,670 --> 00:13:30,870
I wasn't born this way. It was an injury.

265
00:13:31,550 --> 00:13:33,750
When I was ten, I was playing downstairs

266
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:35,120
when I ran into this little punk.

267
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:37,150
He sprayed sparks from a lit sparkler
into my face.

268
00:13:37,150 --> 00:13:38,200
Just my luck.

269
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,400
Both my corneas
were destroyed on the spot.

270
00:13:42,870 --> 00:13:44,030
That's awful.

271
00:13:44,550 --> 00:13:45,790
D-Did they catch the kid?

272
00:13:45,790 --> 00:13:46,670
They did.

273
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:47,670
But that didn't help.

274
00:13:47,670 --> 00:13:49,600
His family was even poorer than mine.

275
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:53,270
They couldn't have paid for the damage,
even if they'd sold everything they owned.

276
00:13:53,270 --> 00:13:54,270
If you'd gone to a big city,

277
00:13:54,270 --> 00:13:56,270
to a major hospital back then,

278
00:13:56,550 --> 00:13:57,390
could things have turned out differently?

279
00:13:57,390 --> 00:13:58,920
Could it have been treated?

280
00:13:59,870 --> 00:14:02,070
There's no point dwelling on what-ifs.

281
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,510
Besides,

282
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,910
it's been so many years.

283
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:08,880
It's probably too late for treatment now.

284
00:14:15,630 --> 00:14:16,200
Careful.

285
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,000
Let me move it out of your way

286
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:17,550
before we go.

287
00:14:17,550 --> 00:14:18,720
I'm fine, I'm fine.

288
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:19,390
Really,

289
00:14:19,550 --> 00:14:20,390
you don't have to.

290
00:14:20,390 --> 00:14:21,670
I'm used to this.

291
00:14:23,790 --> 00:14:25,240
It's okay. I can manage.

292
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:35,630
Well,

293
00:14:38,390 --> 00:14:39,630
if you'd like,

294
00:14:39,790 --> 00:14:41,200
I could walk you home every day.

295
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:41,910
That way,

296
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:44,240
you wouldn't

297
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,320
have to go through so much on your own.

298
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,720
And it'd be safer, right?

299
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:48,240
My dad

300
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:50,870
wanted to pick me up
and drop me off every day, too.

301
00:14:50,870 --> 00:14:52,600
You know why I wouldn't let him?

302
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:55,240
W-Why?

303
00:14:55,750 --> 00:14:57,550
Because one day, he'll grow old.

304
00:14:58,240 --> 00:15:00,100
One day, he won't be here anymore.

305
00:15:01,030 --> 00:15:02,890
Sooner or later, I'll be on my own.

306
00:15:07,150 --> 00:15:08,910
If I learn to live alone now,

307
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:11,730
I won't have to fear anyone leaving me.

308
00:15:31,630 --> 00:15:32,510
I'm home.

309
00:15:34,550 --> 00:15:35,480
Look over there.

310
00:15:42,030 --> 00:15:43,560
On the day I was discharged,

311
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:44,960
I told my dad

312
00:15:45,910 --> 00:15:48,170
I'd never wait for someone
to come get me.

313
00:15:48,790 --> 00:15:50,190
I'd go wherever I wanted,

314
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,910
all on my own.

315
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,860
I don't have many choices in life,

316
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:59,240
so whenever I do have one,

317
00:16:00,030 --> 00:16:01,630
I'll take the initiative.

318
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,440
I'll never just sit around and wait.

319
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:11,650
Liu Zhengguang,

320
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:14,180
thanks for walking me home today.

321
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:17,270
But you don't have to do it again.

322
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:58,200
I'm busy.

323
00:17:09,030 --> 00:17:09,829
How is it?

324
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:11,829
How am I supposed to tell
from just one bite?

325
00:17:11,829 --> 00:17:12,589
Give me two more pieces to try.

326
00:17:12,589 --> 00:17:13,270
Oh, come on.

327
00:17:13,270 --> 00:17:14,480
You're just supposed
to check the seasoning.

328
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:15,410
Rainbow Pillar,

329
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:16,640
dinner's ready.

330
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:17,310
Coming!

331
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,540
Go get Ai Chen for me, will you?

332
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,310
Sure.

333
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:26,750
Sweetheart,

334
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,880
dinner's ready!

335
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:29,880
Got it.

336
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:30,610
Come with me.

337
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:39,860
[Crash Course in Literacy:
Instructional Talk]

338
00:17:43,830 --> 00:17:45,230
The timing's just right.

339
00:17:45,510 --> 00:17:46,310
Chen.

340
00:17:48,270 --> 00:17:49,070
Zhengguang.

341
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,310
Auntie, Uncle.

342
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,830
Have you seen Liu Zhengliang?

343
00:17:52,830 --> 00:17:53,920
He's not answering his phone,

344
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:54,920
and he's not home.

345
00:17:55,270 --> 00:17:56,680
He must be at the hospital.

346
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:57,810
Try calling Junnan.

347
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:00,160
He's already back at work?
He just got back!

348
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,400
Why not?

349
00:18:02,310 --> 00:18:03,970
He's so dedicated to his work.

350
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,100
Have you eaten?

351
00:18:05,110 --> 00:18:06,200
Come join us.

352
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:06,920
No, thanks, Auntie.

353
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:07,720
I'm not hungry.

354
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:08,580
I'll get going.

355
00:18:09,030 --> 00:18:09,830
Don't go!

356
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,650
Your Auntie Si made dumplings.

357
00:18:35,110 --> 00:18:36,170
Is there any for me?

358
00:18:46,350 --> 00:18:47,310
What is it?

359
00:18:47,510 --> 00:18:48,960
What do you mean, what is it?

360
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:50,070
You seem a little down,

361
00:18:50,070 --> 00:18:50,720
with that long face.

362
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:51,920
Just checking on you.

363
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,510
Seriously, can you go back
to your usual self?

364
00:18:54,510 --> 00:18:55,720
I'm not used to this.

365
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,030
Remember

366
00:19:04,590 --> 00:19:06,270
what Mom said one Dragon Boat Festival?

367
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:07,200
Something

368
00:19:07,550 --> 00:19:08,720
about dumplings.

369
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,030
Yeah.

370
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:12,960
She said

371
00:19:13,270 --> 00:19:15,240
she'd learn to make dumplings herself.

372
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:16,590
And from then on,

373
00:19:16,590 --> 00:19:18,270
the dumplings every year
were especially good.

374
00:19:18,270 --> 00:19:19,400
That's not the line.

375
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:25,680
She said

376
00:19:26,590 --> 00:19:27,400
that since I came home

377
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,000
only in the summer each year,

378
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:30,070
the Dragon Boat Festival

379
00:19:30,070 --> 00:19:32,000
was our family's Spring Festival.

380
00:19:32,030 --> 00:19:34,510
And you have to eat dumplings
at Spring Festival,

381
00:19:34,510 --> 00:19:35,310
right?

382
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:39,680
You actually remember that.

383
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,030
Of course I do.

384
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:42,240
It's not like I don't have a heart.

385
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:42,880
Then why do you act

386
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,400
like you don't?

387
00:19:47,790 --> 00:19:48,590
Fine,

388
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,940
I'll stop pretending.

389
00:19:51,270 --> 00:19:52,550
You've seen right through me.

390
00:19:52,550 --> 00:19:53,440
I am human.

391
00:19:56,030 --> 00:19:57,090
Round of applause.

392
00:19:57,790 --> 00:19:59,160
Congratulations on realizing

393
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,160
you're human.

394
00:20:00,550 --> 00:20:01,550
How would you like me to play along?

395
00:20:01,550 --> 00:20:02,720
Should I... should I celebrate with you?

396
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:04,440
Hooray! My brother is human!

397
00:20:04,830 --> 00:20:05,680
Hooray!

398
00:20:11,110 --> 00:20:11,840
Zhengguang.

399
00:20:12,550 --> 00:20:14,350
It's been so long
since you last called me big brother.

400
00:20:14,350 --> 00:20:15,160
Really?

401
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:17,000
I... I didn't even realize.

402
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:21,720
Have some while they're still hot.

403
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:22,590
They're delicious.

404
00:20:22,590 --> 00:20:24,120
They taste just like Mom's.

405
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:25,920
You know why?

406
00:20:27,270 --> 00:20:28,070
Why?

407
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:31,000
Because Mom never actually learned
to make them.

408
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:31,720
Every year,

409
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:32,790
she'd get them from Aunt Mi Si,

410
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:33,880
then tell you

411
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:35,280
she'd made them herself.

412
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,160
Guess I didn't know

413
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:43,270
Mom as well as I thought.

414
00:20:43,270 --> 00:20:44,000
Same here.

415
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:45,590
I didn't know Dad either.

416
00:20:45,590 --> 00:20:47,120
I never even got to meet him.

417
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,750
My memories of him

418
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:52,530
are pretty vague, too.

419
00:20:53,070 --> 00:20:54,670
Not much clearer than yours.

420
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:09,610
Zhengliang,

421
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,350
I miss her.

422
00:21:12,590 --> 00:21:13,400
I mean, Mom.

423
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:16,510
Me too.

424
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,710
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

425
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:26,920
It's the third day after surgery.

426
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,720
The patient is fully conscious.

427
00:21:29,310 --> 00:21:30,240
His Glasgow Coma Scale score

428
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:31,350
is 14,

429
00:21:32,070 --> 00:21:34,240
so he can communicate
without much difficulty.

430
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:34,880
He reports

431
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:36,440
mild pain at the wound site,

432
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,920
with no nausea or vomiting.

433
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:41,790
-Who's that?
-The patient's vital signs are stable.

434
00:21:41,790 --> 00:21:44,190
-His ex-wife.
-His temperature is 36.8 °C.

435
00:21:44,310 --> 00:21:45,110
Good.

436
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:47,260
Movement in all four limbs is normal.

437
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:49,270
Left-sided muscle strength

438
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:51,000
has improved to 4+.

439
00:21:51,270 --> 00:21:53,440
His latest blood count
and electrolyte levels

440
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:55,100
are all within normal ranges.

441
00:22:05,070 --> 00:22:06,240
Dr. Che has already explained

442
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:07,840
his condition to you, right?

443
00:22:09,030 --> 00:22:10,070
The surgery to treat his injuries

444
00:22:10,070 --> 00:22:10,930
went very well.

445
00:22:11,070 --> 00:22:13,270
We also successfully removed the hematoma

446
00:22:13,270 --> 00:22:15,110
and the remaining foreign objects.

447
00:22:15,110 --> 00:22:15,680
But

448
00:22:15,680 --> 00:22:17,030
his preoperative CT scan

449
00:22:17,030 --> 00:22:19,490
suggested an abnormality inside his skull.

450
00:22:20,550 --> 00:22:21,510
Postoperative MRI

451
00:22:21,510 --> 00:22:23,700
and pathology results confirmed

452
00:22:23,830 --> 00:22:25,440
that he has a malignant tumor

453
00:22:25,830 --> 00:22:28,270
in his right temporal lobe.

454
00:22:30,070 --> 00:22:31,960
I believe this may well be

455
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:34,640
why his personality
changed so drastically.

456
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:35,350
So he'll need

457
00:22:35,350 --> 00:22:37,880
another operation

458
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:39,440
to remove the tumor.

459
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:42,680
Of course, not right away.

460
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:43,350
Once his surgical wound

461
00:22:43,350 --> 00:22:45,030
has healed,

462
00:22:46,110 --> 00:22:47,680
we can plan to proceed with the operation

463
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:48,920
as soon as possible.

464
00:22:49,110 --> 00:22:51,910
Otherwise, it could
shorten his life expectancy.

465
00:22:59,590 --> 00:23:01,390
But I don't have much money left.

466
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:03,110
The money I paid before

467
00:23:03,110 --> 00:23:04,310
was all borrowed.

468
00:23:05,350 --> 00:23:06,830
No matter how much more
I scrape together,

469
00:23:06,830 --> 00:23:09,360
I can only manage
ten or twenty thousand yuan.

470
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:11,030
What if that's not enough

471
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:13,210
for another operation?

472
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:15,550
Doesn't he

473
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:17,640
have any other family?

474
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:19,510
No.

475
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,830
We have a child together.

476
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:23,330
Three years old.

477
00:23:24,110 --> 00:23:25,910
The child usually lives with me.

478
00:23:26,830 --> 00:23:28,680
How long have you been divorced?

479
00:23:30,030 --> 00:23:31,070
Less than a year.

480
00:23:37,830 --> 00:23:38,790
I understand.

481
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:39,920
If you have any reservations

482
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:41,070
about the surgery,

483
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:42,200
or...

484
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:47,920
if you don't want
to take responsibility for him anymore,

485
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:49,320
you can tell me directly.

486
00:23:57,920 --> 00:23:58,880
Actually,

487
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:02,310
he used to be such a kind person,

488
00:24:02,590 --> 00:24:04,320
and he had a really good temper.

489
00:24:06,830 --> 00:24:09,350
Then he started getting
more and more irritable.

490
00:24:09,350 --> 00:24:10,550
I kept wondering

491
00:24:10,790 --> 00:24:12,190
why he'd changed so much.

492
00:24:14,270 --> 00:24:15,640
Turns out he was sick.

493
00:24:17,550 --> 00:24:18,680
No wonder

494
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:21,280
he'd be fine one moment
and irritable the next.

495
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:30,360
He was the one who asked for the divorce.

496
00:24:30,790 --> 00:24:33,120
He brought it up
as soon as he was admitted.

497
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:38,030
He just didn't want

498
00:24:38,030 --> 00:24:40,240
to drag me and our child down, did he?

499
00:24:44,350 --> 00:24:45,400
Dr. Liu,

500
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,530
could you please think of
some way to save him?

501
00:24:49,790 --> 00:24:51,270
He's a good man.

502
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:57,880
He really is.

503
00:25:03,110 --> 00:25:03,880
President,

504
00:25:04,070 --> 00:25:05,480
didn't you say

505
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:07,920
Du Fang could be a good publicity angle?

506
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:09,030
Here we go again.

507
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:11,480
Zhang Jiao only got a partial waiver.

508
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:13,030
You want this one completely free?

509
00:25:13,030 --> 00:25:14,830
You can't expect everything
to go your way.

510
00:25:14,830 --> 00:25:16,230
This isn't a charity.

511
00:25:18,030 --> 00:25:20,240
You were the one
who sent me to do the interview, right?

512
00:25:20,240 --> 00:25:21,030
I did it.

513
00:25:21,030 --> 00:25:21,920
And now you're telling me

514
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:22,980
to just let him die?

515
00:25:23,070 --> 00:25:24,400
Won't that end up becoming

516
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:26,030
a case of medical malpractice?

517
00:25:26,030 --> 00:25:29,030
Xiaoximen Hospital is on the verge
of being shut down.

518
00:25:29,030 --> 00:25:30,830
I'm just trying to keep it alive.

519
00:25:31,310 --> 00:25:32,030
Dr. Liu,

520
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:35,030
there are plenty of people in this world
who can't afford medical care.

521
00:25:35,030 --> 00:25:37,030
I've already done everything I can.

522
00:25:39,350 --> 00:25:40,830
Then why don't you sign off on it first?

523
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:43,620
[Decision-Making Procedure for
"Three Major and One Important" Matters]

524
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:42,960
We can put his medical bills
on hold for now.

525
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:44,640
The hospital's going under anyway.

526
00:25:44,640 --> 00:25:46,640
What's one more unpaid bill, right?

527
00:25:48,350 --> 00:25:49,720
Y-You can't keep milking the same target

528
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:51,790
over and over.

529
00:25:53,590 --> 00:25:55,050
President, let me do this.

530
00:25:55,310 --> 00:25:55,830
Let me.

531
00:25:56,750 --> 00:26:00,130
[Decision-Making Procedure for
"Three Major and One Important" Matters]

532
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:00,350
President,

533
00:26:00,550 --> 00:26:02,610
could you please think of something?

534
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:04,240
You're resourceful.

535
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:06,260
I'm sure you'll find a way, right?

536
00:26:06,830 --> 00:26:07,590
I promise

537
00:26:08,350 --> 00:26:09,880
this will be the last time.

538
00:26:10,510 --> 00:26:11,310
Please?

539
00:26:12,070 --> 00:26:13,240
Oh, give me a break.

540
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:22,920
Anyway,

541
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:24,070
I saw you last time.

542
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:25,240
You were secretly watching

543
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:26,350
girl group dance videos in your office.

544
00:26:26,350 --> 00:26:27,110
That won't work.

545
00:26:27,110 --> 00:26:28,240
Not a chance.

546
00:26:30,750 --> 00:26:33,810
You snuck in and watched
for ages yourself, didn't you?

547
00:26:43,110 --> 00:26:44,770
Before I came back to Fucheng,

548
00:26:45,310 --> 00:26:46,110
I met a patient

549
00:26:46,110 --> 00:26:47,680
with high-grade glioma.

550
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:51,040
He was even younger than Du Fang,

551
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:54,170
but there was nothing
we could do but wait for the end.

552
00:26:56,590 --> 00:26:58,590
There was nothing I could do for him.

553
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:00,920
But this patient still has a chance.

554
00:27:03,030 --> 00:27:04,290
Please, think it over.

555
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:07,640
Tens of thousands of yuan
could save a life.

556
00:27:07,880 --> 00:27:08,640
And he's dealing with

557
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:11,240
both a gunshot wound
and a temporal lobe tumor.

558
00:27:40,830 --> 00:27:42,160
Now that you mention it,

559
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:44,830
there might be a way.

560
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:49,000
But you'll have to give up

561
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,550
control over his treatment.

562
00:27:50,550 --> 00:27:51,830
As long as we can save his life,

563
00:27:51,830 --> 00:27:53,690
I don't care about anything else.

564
00:28:07,020 --> 00:28:10,770
[Massage Clinic Run
by Blind Practitioners]

565
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:08,830
Take care.

566
00:28:13,830 --> 00:28:14,550
Jia,

567
00:28:15,240 --> 00:28:16,440
what brings you here?

568
00:28:18,750 --> 00:28:19,830
I asked him to come.

569
00:28:34,160 --> 00:28:35,200
The Taoist asked,

570
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:37,030
"Was General Yang Zaixing

571
00:28:37,030 --> 00:28:39,350
your ancestor?"

572
00:28:39,790 --> 00:28:43,190
Yang Tiexin replied,
"He was my great-great-grandfather."

573
00:28:43,270 --> 00:28:44,400
The next part goes…

574
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:47,750
The Taoist immediately showed his respect

575
00:28:47,830 --> 00:28:49,400
and clasped his hands in greeting.

576
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:52,440
"I mistook you two for villains just now.

577
00:28:52,590 --> 00:28:54,120
Please forgive my offense.

578
00:28:54,310 --> 00:28:57,240
I see now that you are descendants
of a loyal and honorable family.

579
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:58,720
I sincerely apologize.

580
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:01,680
May I ask your esteemed name?"

581
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:09,640
Why did you stop reading?

582
00:29:13,510 --> 00:29:14,310
Well,

583
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:16,720
I'd never imagined

584
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:18,780
anyone would think I had a nice voice.

585
00:29:20,790 --> 00:29:22,070
When we first met,

586
00:29:22,070 --> 00:29:23,930
you even said I was good-looking.

587
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:26,270
It was the first time anyone

588
00:29:26,270 --> 00:29:28,070
had ever said that about me, too.

589
00:29:29,920 --> 00:29:31,320
You heard that part, too.

590
00:29:33,310 --> 00:29:34,880
Am I your type?

591
00:29:39,790 --> 00:29:40,720
I'm teasing you.

592
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:42,550
Go on reading.

593
00:29:47,550 --> 00:29:49,000
Guo Xiaotian said,

594
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:50,590
"Think nothing of it!

595
00:29:50,590 --> 00:29:52,440
Please, come inside, Taoist priest,

596
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:54,240
and join us for three more cups."

597
00:29:54,350 --> 00:29:56,640
At this point, Yang Tiexin
and Guo Xiaotian

598
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:57,900
felt a little awkward,

599
00:29:58,070 --> 00:29:58,640
you know?

600
00:29:58,640 --> 00:30:00,300
They'd just beaten the man up.

601
00:30:00,310 --> 00:30:01,310
And the Taoist priest

602
00:30:01,310 --> 00:30:03,310
wasn't one to hold a grudge.

603
00:30:04,030 --> 00:30:05,400
As he picked up his spear,

604
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:06,440
the Taoist priest said,

605
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,170
"Excellent!

606
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:10,680
I was just hoping
to have a good drink with you two!"

607
00:30:20,370 --> 00:30:22,780
[Starry Night]

608
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:32,550
♪ You belong to me ♪

609
00:30:32,980 --> 00:30:34,570
♪ I belong to— ♪

610
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:34,680
Everyone's here.

611
00:30:34,790 --> 00:30:36,350
So, Huang, are you done
with your handover?

612
00:30:36,350 --> 00:30:37,310
All done. I'm off work.

613
00:30:37,310 --> 00:30:39,350
Yang got here early.
He's already handed over.

614
00:30:39,350 --> 00:30:40,160
Well,

615
00:30:40,270 --> 00:30:41,070
um,

616
00:30:41,880 --> 00:30:43,680
after things settle down a bit,

617
00:30:44,030 --> 00:30:45,480
I'd like to treat everyone

618
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:46,550
to a meal.

619
00:30:47,200 --> 00:30:48,330
You're treating us?

620
00:30:48,550 --> 00:30:49,350
What for?

621
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:51,310
W-Well, I left,

622
00:30:51,310 --> 00:30:52,480
but now I'm back.

623
00:30:52,720 --> 00:30:53,400
I've caused everyone

624
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:54,930
a lot of trouble, haven't I?

625
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:56,030
So,

626
00:30:56,310 --> 00:30:57,310
j-just a small gathering.

627
00:30:57,310 --> 00:30:58,160
A small one.

628
00:30:58,160 --> 00:30:58,830
Just the few of us

629
00:30:58,830 --> 00:30:59,760
from the office,

630
00:30:59,790 --> 00:31:02,030
plus Ai Chen and my younger brother.

631
00:31:04,720 --> 00:31:05,470
Dr. Liu.

632
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:07,440
I-I have to give you a hug.

633
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:09,480
J-Just let me know

634
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:10,480
the date in advance.

635
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:11,790
I'll have Li reserve a large private room.

636
00:31:11,790 --> 00:31:12,440
No need,

637
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:13,110
Huang.

638
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:15,360
I'll take care of everything this time.

639
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:18,110
You're really on top
of everything now, huh?

640
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:19,310
Absolutely perfect.

641
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:19,960
All right,

642
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:20,960
I'll wait to hear from you.

643
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:21,640
See you.

644
00:31:21,750 --> 00:31:22,440
-I'm off.
-Bye-bye. Bye-bye.

645
00:31:22,440 --> 00:31:23,110
I'm heading out first.

646
00:31:23,110 --> 00:31:23,880
Look at you, Zhengliang.

647
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:24,920
You're making progress!

648
00:31:24,920 --> 00:31:26,980
I've been looking forward to it, too.

649
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:28,660
Anyway, I'd better get going.

650
00:31:30,590 --> 00:31:31,240
Bye-bye.

651
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:34,800
Am I really that perfect?

652
00:31:46,400 --> 00:31:47,460
What are you doing?

653
00:31:50,270 --> 00:31:52,000
I didn't sleep well last night.

654
00:31:52,350 --> 00:31:53,410
I'm a little tired.

655
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:55,530
I'm getting sleepy.

656
00:31:58,110 --> 00:31:59,240
Have you guys heard?

657
00:31:59,350 --> 00:32:00,830
Our hospital's shutting down.

658
00:31:59,770 --> 00:32:09,500
[Triage Desk]

659
00:32:01,070 --> 00:32:01,960
Wasn't that just a rumor?

660
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:03,760
Director Li denied it last week.

661
00:32:03,830 --> 00:32:05,270
And you just believe him?

662
00:32:05,350 --> 00:32:06,240
I heard

663
00:32:06,350 --> 00:32:08,550
it's definitely closing within 2 months.

664
00:32:08,550 --> 00:32:09,270
What?

665
00:32:09,270 --> 00:32:11,350
Then what are we supposed
to do about our jobs?

666
00:32:09,550 --> 00:32:17,000
[Hospital Oversight
and Complaints Hotline]

667
00:32:11,790 --> 00:32:12,920
Apparently,

668
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:14,030
about one in ten of us

669
00:32:14,030 --> 00:32:15,240
can transfer to No. 6 Hospital.

670
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:16,790
And the rest will be laid off?

671
00:32:16,790 --> 00:32:17,640
Ying,

672
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:21,930
[Patient Satisfaction Survey]

673
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:19,000
are you sure about this?

674
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,130
I'm almost certain.

675
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:20,920
Dr. Chen's here.

676
00:32:20,920 --> 00:32:21,750
Dr. Chen, come here.

677
00:32:21,750 --> 00:32:22,480
Well...

678
00:32:22,010 --> 00:32:28,480
[No smoking]

679
00:32:22,590 --> 00:32:23,400
Junnan,

680
00:32:23,550 --> 00:32:25,680
is our hospital really shutting down?

681
00:32:25,790 --> 00:32:27,000
So what if it is?

682
00:32:27,270 --> 00:32:28,600
We can all stop working.

683
00:32:28,830 --> 00:32:30,030
Then we won't have to see
each other anymore. Sounds great to me.

684
00:32:30,030 --> 00:32:32,030
Oh, it's over. It's 100% confirmed.

685
00:32:57,750 --> 00:32:58,350
Morning.

686
00:33:09,310 --> 00:33:10,540
I'll go buy some.

687
00:33:11,270 --> 00:33:12,000
Give it to me.

688
00:33:18,790 --> 00:33:20,190
There's still some left.

689
00:33:21,110 --> 00:33:22,710
You're pretty resourceful.

690
00:33:22,720 --> 00:33:24,720
I'll buy some on my way back tonight.

691
00:33:35,720 --> 00:33:36,650
Liu Zhengliang,

692
00:33:38,070 --> 00:33:39,800
do you think I have a nice voice?

693
00:33:46,030 --> 00:33:46,830
It's not bad,

694
00:33:47,440 --> 00:33:48,840
but it's not good either.

695
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:51,440
Why?

696
00:33:51,590 --> 00:33:52,920
You want to be a host?

697
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:55,090
I want to be a singer.

698
00:33:58,920 --> 00:33:59,640
Liu Zhengguang,

699
00:33:59,640 --> 00:34:00,920
stop making me laugh.

700
00:34:01,350 --> 00:34:02,030
If you can sing,

701
00:34:02,030 --> 00:34:03,240
then pigs can fly.

702
00:34:03,790 --> 00:34:05,640
I was obviously talking nonsense,

703
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:07,700
but you just had to keep picking on me.

704
00:34:08,630 --> 00:34:10,320
Sorry. Reflex.

705
00:34:15,710 --> 00:34:16,510
Zhengguang,

706
00:34:19,840 --> 00:34:21,840
whatever you want to do in the future,

707
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:22,960
I'll support you.

708
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:25,730
Because I'm your only brother.

709
00:34:34,070 --> 00:34:35,000
You know,

710
00:34:35,440 --> 00:34:37,110
maybe you should go back
to being yourself.

711
00:34:37,110 --> 00:34:38,909
You really don't have to do this.

712
00:34:39,030 --> 00:34:40,830
You're fine just the way you are.

713
00:34:41,030 --> 00:34:42,030
No way.

714
00:34:42,550 --> 00:34:43,320
I've already said I'd do it,

715
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:44,650
so I have to keep my word.

716
00:34:47,190 --> 00:34:48,440
Could you not say that

717
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:49,510
while I'm brushing my teeth?

718
00:34:49,510 --> 00:34:50,480
It's making me sick.

719
00:34:50,480 --> 00:34:51,840
Is your stomach upset?

720
00:34:52,190 --> 00:34:53,989
Want me to get you some medicine?

721
00:34:54,630 --> 00:34:55,840
I'm kidding.

722
00:35:02,030 --> 00:35:03,070
So am I.

723
00:35:10,150 --> 00:35:10,960
Sweetheart,

724
00:35:11,590 --> 00:35:12,800
what's wrong?

725
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:15,190
D-Do you need to go to the hospital?

726
00:35:15,190 --> 00:35:16,150
No, no.

727
00:35:18,070 --> 00:35:20,800
Did you eat something
that didn't agree with you?

728
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:22,150
It's not that.

729
00:35:22,880 --> 00:35:25,280
This has happened before.

730
00:35:44,400 --> 00:35:45,070
I'm fine.

731
00:35:45,070 --> 00:35:47,270
Maybe the cold air irritated my throat.

732
00:36:05,710 --> 00:36:07,760
Look at you! You've thrown up,

733
00:36:09,150 --> 00:36:10,480
and your face is so pale.

734
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:11,760
It's fine.

735
00:36:11,960 --> 00:36:15,090
Here, drink some water.
It'll help settle your stomach.

736
00:36:16,630 --> 00:36:17,630
I feel better.

737
00:36:25,430 --> 00:36:27,680
[Crash Course in Literacy:
Instructional Talk]

738
00:36:28,550 --> 00:36:30,810
Did Liu Zhengliang say something to you?

739
00:36:32,670 --> 00:36:34,000
I just wanted to try learning on my own.

740
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:34,800
No way.

741
00:36:35,510 --> 00:36:37,670
You've tried learning before, remember?

742
00:36:37,670 --> 00:36:39,800
You were throwing up so badly
you almost brought up bile.

743
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:41,550
You swore you'd never study again.

744
00:36:41,550 --> 00:36:42,400
Over the years,

745
00:36:42,400 --> 00:36:43,320
you've gotten more and more

746
00:36:43,320 --> 00:36:44,780
used to being illiterate.

747
00:36:44,880 --> 00:36:46,030
Why would you suddenly

748
00:36:46,030 --> 00:36:47,960
want to learn again after one trip out?

749
00:36:47,960 --> 00:36:49,420
It must be Liu Zhengliang.

750
00:36:50,510 --> 00:36:51,440
I'm telling you,

751
00:36:52,510 --> 00:36:53,920
if he looks down on you,

752
00:36:54,630 --> 00:36:56,560
you absolutely cannot be with him.

753
00:36:57,110 --> 00:36:57,960
Understand?

754
00:37:02,920 --> 00:37:04,800
I really did want to try on my own.

755
00:37:13,550 --> 00:37:15,960
I haven't really gone anywhere
in all these years.

756
00:37:15,960 --> 00:37:17,320
I was scared, you know.

757
00:37:20,070 --> 00:37:22,150
And I couldn't be bothered

758
00:37:22,150 --> 00:37:24,210
to explain everything to strangers.

759
00:37:25,190 --> 00:37:26,510
But on this trip,

760
00:37:26,510 --> 00:37:28,320
I found something that works pretty well:

761
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:29,980
pretending to be a foreigner.

762
00:37:30,630 --> 00:37:31,760
Oh no...

763
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:33,550
What do I do?

764
00:37:37,590 --> 00:37:39,450
Which line am I supposed to get in?

765
00:37:46,820 --> 00:37:47,690
Hello.

766
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:48,400
Hello.

767
00:37:49,760 --> 00:37:51,230
This, this...

768
00:37:51,710 --> 00:37:53,910
I can't understand a single thing here.

769
00:37:54,840 --> 00:37:56,110
It's pretty convincing.

770
00:37:56,110 --> 00:37:56,840
Really.

771
00:37:59,590 --> 00:38:00,400
But

772
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:04,230
I've been thinking,

773
00:38:07,280 --> 00:38:09,740
I can't go on like this
for the rest of my life,

774
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:10,710
can I?

775
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:17,710
I want to be able to read

776
00:38:17,710 --> 00:38:19,440
what's on my boarding pass.

777
00:38:23,710 --> 00:38:25,480
And I want to understand

778
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:28,230
what's written

779
00:38:28,230 --> 00:38:29,890
on those delivery boxes, too.

780
00:38:31,030 --> 00:38:32,920
When people text me,

781
00:38:33,320 --> 00:38:34,150
I want to be able to text them

782
00:38:34,150 --> 00:38:35,440
back and forth,

783
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:36,190
you know?

784
00:38:36,230 --> 00:38:38,000
Share what's really on my mind.

785
00:38:43,070 --> 00:38:44,400
So Liu Zhengliang

786
00:38:44,510 --> 00:38:46,970
never rubbed my illiteracy
in my face at all.

787
00:38:49,030 --> 00:38:51,400
If anything, I feel like
his coming back

788
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:52,840
has inspired me.

789
00:38:53,960 --> 00:38:56,290
His condition
was more serious than mine.

790
00:38:56,760 --> 00:38:57,760
He's still willing to try.

791
00:38:57,760 --> 00:38:58,920
So why can't I?

792
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:06,800
President.

793
00:39:06,200 --> 00:39:10,160
[Healing pain with compassion,
lighting up hope with dedication]

794
00:39:07,150 --> 00:39:08,000
You're here.

795
00:39:08,710 --> 00:39:10,570
Let me introduce everyone to you.

796
00:39:11,320 --> 00:39:12,520
Chief Physician Qin,

797
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:14,190
a neurosurgeon

798
00:39:14,480 --> 00:39:15,610
from No. 1 Hospital.

799
00:39:15,800 --> 00:39:16,230
Hello.

800
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:17,000
Hello.

801
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:17,920
Chief Physician Qin

802
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:19,320
is the top neurosurgeon

803
00:39:20,150 --> 00:39:21,840
in Fucheng.

804
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:23,440
You're too kind.

805
00:39:23,440 --> 00:39:24,480
Everyone here is part

806
00:39:24,480 --> 00:39:26,210
of Chief Physician Qin's team.

807
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:27,690
They're all top-notch.

808
00:39:28,230 --> 00:39:29,890
All right, let's get started.

809
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:32,280
Associate Chief Physician Liu

810
00:39:32,280 --> 00:39:33,400
certainly has an air of authority.

811
00:39:33,400 --> 00:39:34,090
You can tell he's the one

812
00:39:34,090 --> 00:39:35,380
who gives the orders.

813
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:38,800
And you are?

814
00:39:39,070 --> 00:39:40,470
My name is Ye Zhengqiang.

815
00:39:43,630 --> 00:39:44,590
I was just organizing some documents,

816
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:45,590
so I'm a little late.

817
00:39:45,590 --> 00:39:46,550
some documents.

818
00:39:46,920 --> 00:39:48,320
Let me introduce myself.

819
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:49,670
I'm Liu Zhengliang,

820
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,190
an ordinary doctor

821
00:39:51,190 --> 00:39:52,520
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

822
00:39:53,070 --> 00:39:54,000
Thank you all

823
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:55,730
for stepping in to help Du Fang.

824
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:58,230
As long as you cover

825
00:39:58,230 --> 00:39:59,630
all of Du Fang's medical expenses

826
00:39:59,630 --> 00:40:00,710
this time,

827
00:40:02,550 --> 00:40:03,960
we'll even have our President Long

828
00:40:03,960 --> 00:40:05,070
get onto the table and dance for you

829
00:40:05,070 --> 00:40:06,990
or perform a sing-and-dance duet
Whatever you like.

830
00:40:06,990 --> 00:40:15,350
[Healing pain with compassion,
lighting up hope with dedication]

831
00:40:07,320 --> 00:40:09,190
Who'd want to see President Long dance?

832
00:40:09,190 --> 00:40:10,800
Well, I can dance if needed.

833
00:40:10,920 --> 00:40:11,920
I wanna see. I wanna see.

834
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:12,670
You...

835
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:15,940
Look how supportive
Chief Physician Qin is!

836
00:40:16,070 --> 00:40:17,920
All right, enough joking around.

837
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:19,450
Let me say a few words first.

838
00:40:19,800 --> 00:40:21,800
Du Fang's case

839
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:23,070
is rather unusual.

840
00:40:23,550 --> 00:40:24,840
He's agreed

841
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:26,070
to join our team's

842
00:40:26,070 --> 00:40:27,630
clinical trial

843
00:40:27,630 --> 00:40:29,070
for temporal lobe tumors

844
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:30,070
and has signed

845
00:40:30,070 --> 00:40:31,600
the informed consent form.

846
00:40:33,070 --> 00:40:35,630
The treatment costs

847
00:40:35,630 --> 00:40:36,920
will be covered

848
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:38,880
by our department's research funds.

849
00:40:38,880 --> 00:40:40,920
All research findings from this case

850
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:43,400
will be owned

851
00:40:43,440 --> 00:40:44,280
by the neurosurgery team

852
00:40:44,280 --> 00:40:46,000
at No. 1 Hospital.

853
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:49,410
President Long,

854
00:40:49,670 --> 00:40:50,880
does your hospital

855
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:52,710
have any objections?

856
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:53,880
